    faqs: [
      { question: "Can I sell old electronics in Kochi?", answer: "Yes. Message the device type, condition and photos on WhatsApp for a preliminary quote, then arrange doorstep pickup and payment if you accept it." },
      { question: "What electronics may have resale value?", answer: "Laptops, phones, tablets and some desktop components most commonly have resale value, but it depends on condition and demand — ask about any specific device." },
      { question: "Can broken electronics be sold?", answer: "Yes, non-working devices can still have component or scrap value. Mention the condition honestly when you message." },
      { question: "How is quote value decided?", answer: "Final quote depends on item type, quantity, condition, location and current market rate." },
      { question: "Is the quote guaranteed?", answer: "A preliminary estimate is possible from photos and details, but the final number is confirmed after physical inspection." },
      { question: "What photos should I send?", answer: "Front and back of the device, the screen if applicable, and any visible damage." },
      { question: "Can I sell old laptops?", answer: "Yes, working and non-working laptops are both accepted for a condition-based quote." },
      { question: "Can I sell mobile phones?", answer: "Yes, phones are accepted for resale quotes — mention brand, age and condition." },
      { question: "Can offices sell bulk electronics?", answer: "Yes, message the full list with quantities for a consolidated quote." },
      { question: "What affects old laptop value?", answer: "Working condition, age, specifications, screen and battery health, and whether the original charger is included." },
      { question: "Should I remove data first?", answer: "Yes, ideally before handover. Data destruction support is available if you'd rather not handle it yourself." },
      { question: "Is resale better than recycling?", answer: "For working devices, resale is usually worth checking first since it captures more value than recycling. Non-working or very old devices are often better suited to recycling." },
      { question: "What happens if the item has no value?", answer: "It can still be recycled responsibly at no cost to you — there's no obligation to sell just because you sent details." },
      { question: "Can batteries be sold?", answer: "Batteries are generally handled through battery recycling rather than resale, given the different safety and handling requirements." },
      { question: "Are cables and accessories accepted?", answer: "Yes, and including original accessories like a charger can add a small amount to a device's quote." },
      { question: "Does pickup depend on quantity?", answer: "Pickup feasibility depends on item type, quantity, condition and location." },
      { question: "Is cash guaranteed?", answer: "Payment is arranged once a quote is accepted, confirmed at the time of inspection rather than promised in advance." },
      { question: "What is condition-based value?", answer: "It means the quote reflects the device's actual working status, physical condition and completeness rather than a flat rate by model alone." },
      { question: "How do I avoid unsafe buyers?", answer: "Ask how data is handled before sale, whether documentation is available, and be cautious of a buyer offering a fixed price without ever inspecting the item." },
      { question: "How do I request a quote?", answer: "Message the item type, condition and photos on WhatsApp for a preliminary estimate." },
    ],
